":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_prepare_route","isError":false}]},{"role":"assistant","sequence":28,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan awaiting your approval (`appr_14`). Total cost is $10.22, under the $15.00 policy cap.\n\n| # | Leg | In | Expected out | Cost (USD) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `eth-swap-eth-wbtc` (eth1) | 0.1 ETH | 495,000 WBTC units | 3.90 |\n| 2 | `eth-bridge-wbtc-robinhood` (eth1→rh1) | 247,500 WBTC | 246,666 WBTC | 1.40 |\n| 3 | `eth-bridge-wbtc-arbitrum` (eth1→arb1) | 247,500 WBTC | 246,666 WBTC | 1.40 |\n| 4 | `eth-bridge-eth-robinhood` (gas for rh1) | 0.0003 ETH | ~0.000133 ETH | 1.40 |\n| 5 | `eth-bridge-eth-arbitrum` (gas for arb1) | 0.0003 ETH | ~0.000133 ETH | 1.40 |\n| 6 | `rh-swap-wbtc-eth` (rh1) | 246,666 WBTC | ~0.0492 ETH | 0.36 |\n| 7 | `arb-swap-wbtc-usdc` (arb1) | 246,666 WBTC | ~147.70 USDC | 0.36 |\n\n- **Why bridge first:** the only WBTC→ETH and WBTC→USDC swaps on the target chains run on rh1 and arb1, so the WBTC has to be bridged there first.\n- **Cheaper than the alternative:** swapping to USDC on Ethereum and then bridging would cost about $5.30 for that half, against $1.76 this way.\n- **Why legs 4 and 5 are there:** rh1 and arb1 both hold 0 ETH, and legs 6 and 7 need gas. arb1 also has to keep gas after it ends up holding USDC. I couldn't confirm that a swap fails with zero gas, so this is a precaution. Dropping them saves $2.80 but risks a failed swap. The bridge fee is about 0.000167 ETH, so smaller amounts get rejected as `amount_too_small`.\n- **Split amounts:** the 247,500 split assumes leg 1 returns exactly 495,000. If it returns something different, I'll re-quote legs 2 and 3 before running them.\n- **Execution:** I'll run the legs one at a time and check each destination balance before the next.\n- **Gas on eth1:** it keeps about 0.047 ETH after the route, well above the 0.0003 ETH gas minimum.\n\nApprove to proceed, or set a different cost cap."}]},{"role":"user","sequence":29,"content":[{"type":"text","tex